cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use FeuPy in your research, please cite this software."

title: "FeuPy: Tools for very-high-energy gamma-ray analysis and simulations"

type: software

version: "0.1.0"

authors:
  - family-names: "Costa Jr."
    given-names: "Rubens"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2893-7589"

  - family-names: "dos Anjos"
    given-names: "Rita C."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6463-2272"

license: "BSD-3-Clause"

repository-code: "https://github.com/rubensjrcosta/feupy"

keywords:
  - gamma-ray astronomy
  - very-high-energy gamma rays
  - CTAO
  - Gammapy
  - astrophysics
  - scientific software

abstract: >
  FeuPy is a Python package for very-high-energy gamma-ray analysis
  and simulations. It provides tools for working with gamma-ray source
  catalogs, instrument response functions, sensitivity calculations,
  simulations, visualization, and related astrophysical analyses.
  FeuPy builds on the scientific Python ecosystem and integrates with
  Gammapy for gamma-ray data analysis.